{title: My Soul Thirsts}
{subtitle: Psalms 63:1–3}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Cm] | ×2
| [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O God, you are my God, I seek you at dawn
[F]My heart, [Eb]I seek you [F]at dawn
My [Bb]soul thirsts for [Gm]you in the dry land
My body longs [Bb]for you where there [Cm]is no water
In the wilder[D]ness of [Eb]Judah, I stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]So I have [Gm]gazed on you in the [Eb]sanctu[F]ary
To see your pow[D]er and your glory [Gm]shine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your [F]steadfast [Eb]love is bet[Bb]ter than [Gm]life
My [F]lips will praise you [Eb]with all [Bb]my might
I [Gm]will bless you [F]as long as [Eb]I live
In [Cm]your name, [D]my hands will [Gm]rise
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [F] | [Eb] | [Cm] | ×2
| [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Your [Gm]love is [F]better than the breath of [Eb]life
My [Cm]lips will praise you, they will [Gm]never cease
I will [F]bless you while my [Eb]days remain
In your [Cm]holy name, I [D]find my peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your [Gm]steadfast [F]love is [Eb]better than [Bb]life
My [Gm]lips will [F]praise you with all [Eb]my [Bb]might
I will [Gm]bless you as [F]long as I [Eb]live
In your [Cm]name, my [D]hands will rise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]My [Eb]soul will be [F]satisfied as [Gm]with rich food
With [Eb]joyful [F]lips, my mouth will [D]praise you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You, [Gm]oh God, you are my God, I seek you at [F]dawn
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
